  "summary": "Covenant signs are visible markers that seal and remember God's covenant promises.",
  "historical_context": "Signs such as the rainbow, circumcision, Passover, and the Sabbath mark covenant identity and obligation.",
  "ancient_near_east_context": "Treaty markers and memorials were common in the ancient world, but Scripture gives them theological meaning rather than magical force.",
  "literary_context": "Covenant signs appear at key moments in the biblical storyline and point beyond themselves to promise and obedience.",
  "covenantal_significance": "Covenant signs are means of remembrance, identity, and assurance, never substitutes for faithfulness.",
